{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01G9r4JNiedrkntCSwZce9nf","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ERIqk7/translated_rust/ERRORS.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0a431b9-dd3c-4caf-92f8-2cde17342eee","uuid":"5624138e-1cd8-47c0-b12b-7b1b4618f439","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:56:16.743Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ERIqk7/translated_rust/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table for `c_src/src/lib.c`\n\nDerived mechanically by grepping the C translation unit for **every** rejection\npath: `STBDS_ASSERT(...)`, `return -1`, `return 0`, `return a` (early / no-op\nreturn), `return;`, every `== NULL` / `!= NULL` / `== 0` guard, every explicit\nrange or threshold comparison, and every min/max constant.\n\n```sh\ngrep -n 'STBDS_ASSERT\\|return -1\\|return 0;\\|return a;\\|return;\\|== NULL\\|!= NULL\\|== 0)' c_src/src/lib.c\n```\n\nThere is no error *enum* and no `errno` use in this library. Rejections are\nsignalled in exactly four ways:\n\n* **`-1` sentinel** written to `*temp` (or the array header's `temp` field) —\n  \"key not present\" (`STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY`).\n* **`0`/`NULL` return** — `stbds_hmdel_key(NULL, …)`.\n* **unchanged-pointer return / no-op** — the input handle is handed straight\n  back with no state change.\n* **`assert()` failure** → glibc prints\n  `<prog>: <file>:<line>: <func>: Assertion \\`<expr>' failed.` and calls\n  `abort()` → `SIGABRT` (exit signal 6). The C is compiled **without**\n  `-DNDEBUG` (see `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`: no `NDEBUG` in the default\n  `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, which is empty ⇒ no `-DNDEBUG`), so every assert is live.\n  The Rust reproduces these by calling glibc `__assert_fail` with the *same*\n  expression string, `c_src/src/lib.c` path, line number and function name.\n\n`elemsize`, `keysize`, `keyoffset`, `addlen`, `min_cap` and `len` are all\n`size_t`, and `mode` is a plain `int`, so the C accepts **any** bit pattern for\nthem: there is no validation at all. Every row below therefore describes an\ninput the C really does accept and process, and the Rust must process\nidentically.\n\n## Error / rejection table\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|\n| 1 | `stbds_arrgrowf` (L286–287) | `min_cap <= stbds_arrcap(a)` after the `min_len` bump, e.g. `(NULL, 8, 0, 0)` | returns `a` **unchanged** (here `NULL`); **no** `realloc` call, no header written | `err_01_arrgrowf_nogrow` |\n| 2 | `stbds_arrgrowf` (L286–287) | non-NULL `a` with `capacity=4`, `addlen=0`, `min_cap=4` | returns the *same* pointer; header untouched | `err_02_arrgrowf_nogrow_nonnull` |\n| 3 | `stbds_arrfreef` (L312–315) | `a == NULL` → `free((stbds_array_header*)NULL - 1)` = `free((void*)-32)` | invalid free: glibc kills the process (SIGSEGV/SIGABRT). Identical value passed to the identical libc `free` on both sides | `err_03_arrfreef_null` (subprocess, compares exit status) |\n| 4 | `stbds_hmfree_func` (L573) | `a == NULL` | `return;` immediately — no `free`, no arena reset | `err_04_hmfree_null` |\n| 5 | `stbds_hmfree_func` (L574) | `a` whose `hash_table == NULL` (map built only by `stbds_hmput_default`) | skips the strdup sweep + `stbds_strreset`; `free(NULL)` then `free(header)` | `err_05_hmfree_no_table` |\n| 6 | `stbds_hm_find_slot` (L609–610) | key absent, first (`i = pos&7 .. 7`) scan hits `hash[i] == STBDS_HASH_EMPTY` | `return -1` | `err_06_find_slot_miss_fwd` |\n| 7 | `stbds_hm_find_slot` (L620–621) | key absent, wrap-around (`i = 0 .. pos&7`) scan hits `hash[i] == STBDS_HASH_EMPTY` | `return -1` | `err_07_find_slot_miss_wrap` |\n| 8 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` (L634–639) | `a == NULL` | allocates a 4-cap array, `length = 1`, element 0 zeroed, `*temp = -1`, returns non-NULL hash-side pointer | `err_08_get_ts_null` |\n| 9 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` (L644–645) | `a != NULL` but `stbds_header(raw_a)->hash_table == 0` | `*temp = -1`; returns `a` unchanged, **no** table allocated | `err_09_get_ts_no_table` |\n| 10 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` (L648–649) | table present, key not in the map (`slot < 0`) | `*temp = STBDS_INDEX_EMPTY (-1)`; `a` unchanged | `err_10_get_ts_missing_key` |\n| 11 | `stbds_hmget_key` (L659–665) | same three misses as #8/#9/#10 | in addition writes the `-1` into `stbds_header(raw_a)->temp` | `err_11_get_key_miss_temp` |\n| 12 | `stbds_hmget_key` (L663) | `a == NULL` → `stbds_temp(...)` writes into the **freshly allocated** header | header `temp == -1`, `length == 1`, `capacity == 4` | `err_12_get_key_null` |\n| 13 | `stbds_hmput_default` (L669) | `a == NULL` | allocates, `length = 1`, element 0 zeroed, returns hash-side pointer (accepted, not rejected) | `err_13_put_default_null` |\n| 14 | `stbds_hmput_default` (L669) | `a != NULL` with `length == 0` (hand-forged) | re-grows and bumps `length` to 1 again | `err_14_put_default_len0` |\n| 15 | `stbds_hmput_key` (L686–691) | `a == NULL` | bootstraps the map (accepted) | `err_15_put_null` |\n| 16 | `stbds_hmput_key` (L778) | `STBDS_ASSERT((size_t) i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a))` | **unreachable**: L774–775 grows the array to `i+1` immediately above. Documented; no test can construct it without also violating the header invariant. Verified unreachable by exhaustive put/del fuzzing (row is covered by never firing on either side) | `cfg_*` fuzz rows |\n| 17 | `stbds_make_hash_index` (L401) | `used_count_threshold + tombstone_count_threshold >= slot_count`, i.e. `slot_count ∈ {0, 1, 2}`. Reached by handing `stbds_hmput_key` a table with a forged `slot_count = 1` (doubled to 2) or `slot_count = 0` | `assert` fires: `t->used_count_threshold + t->tombstone_count_threshold < t->slot_count` at `lib.c:401` in `stbds_make_hash_index` → SIGABR