r a self-consistent arena**: the grow branch either returns early (`len > blocksize`) or sets `remaining = blocksize >= len`. Documented; the *reachable* misuse is row #26 | `cfg_*` arena rows |\n| 26 | `stbds_stralloc` (L914) | forged arena `{ storage = NULL, remaining = SIZE_MAX }` → `len <= remaining` so the grow branch is skipped, then `a->storage->storage` dereferences NULL | SIGSEGV on both sides (identical NULL dereference) | `err_26_stralloc_null_storage` (subprocess) |\n| 27 | `stbds_stralloc` (L888) | forged `a->block = 200` → `512u << (200>>1)` = shift count 100 ≥ 64 ⇒ **UB in C**; gcc/x86-64 emits `shl` whose count is taken mod 64 ⇒ `512 << 36` | Rust `wrapping_shl` uses the same mod-64 rule ⇒ identical `blocksize`, identical branch taken | `err_27_stralloc_block_ub` |\n| 28 | `stbds_stralloc` (L890–891) | `a->block` already saturated (`512 << (block>>1) >= 1<<20`, i.e. `block >= 22`) | `++a->block` is **skipped**; `blocksize` stays at the `STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`-capped value | `err_28_stralloc_block_saturated` |\n| 29 | `stbds_strreset` (L920) | `a == NULL` | dereferences NULL → SIGSEGV on both sides | `err_29_strreset_null` (subprocess) |\n| 30 | `stbds_strreset` (L920–930) | already-empty arena (`storage == NULL`) | loop body never runs; `memset(a, 0, 24)` still executed (clears `remaining`/`block`/`mode`) | `err_30_strreset_empty` |\n| 31 | `stbds_hash_bytes` (L553) | `p == NULL, len == 0` | no bytes read; returns the pure seed-derived value; must match exactly | `err_31_hash_bytes_null_zero` |\n| 32 | `stbds_hash_string` (L477–481) | `str` = `\"\"` (immediate NUL) | while-loop never runs; returns the finalisation of `seed ^ seed` | `err_32_hash_string_empty` |\n| 33 | `stbds_hash_string` (L480) | `str == NULL` | dereferences NULL → SIGSEGV on both sides | `err_33_hash_string_null` (subprocess) |\n| 34 | mode as out-of-range enum: `stbds_hmput_key`/`stbds_hmget_key`/`stbds_hm_find_slot` (L560, L590, L713, L732) | `mode = -1` (and `INT_MIN`