51 |\n| delete position | `old_index == final_index` (delete last, no memmove) vs `old_index != final_index` (memmove + re-index) | L839–851 |\n| delete volume | until `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` (⇒ rebuild, same slot_count) and until `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` (⇒ shrink ÷2; shrink threshold forced to 0 when `slot_count <= 8`) | L399–400, L854–862 |\n| reuse of tombstones | put finds a `STBDS_INDEX_DELETED` slot before an empty one ⇒ `pos = tombstone; --tombstone_count` | L739–742, L755–758, L766–769 |\n| `stbds_stralloc` string length | `1` (`\"\"`); `<= remaining`; `> remaining` but `<= blocksize`; `> blocksize` (dedicated oversized block, spliced *after* head when `storage != NULL`, else becomes head with `remaining = 0`) | L885–911 |\n| `strkey` `n` | `0`, positive, negative, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX` | L941 |\n| `intput` `num` | any value ≠ 9, 11 (see `ERRORS.md` #44/#45 for 9 and 11) | L945–956 |\n\n## Configuration table\n\nEvery row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** (fixed seed\n`0xC0FFEE_...`, see `tests/common/mod.rs`) against both `.so`s, comparing:\nheader (`length`, `capacity`, `temp`), all element bytes (keys dereferenced as\nstrings for string modes), and the whole `stbds_hash_index`\n(`slot_count`, `slot_count_log2`, `used_count`, all three thresholds,\n`tombstone_count`, `seed`, `string.{remaining,block,mode}`) plus every\nbucket's `hash[8]` / `index[8]`.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 0`, `p = NULL` and `p` valid; seeds `{0, 1, 0x31415926, SIZE_MAX, random×64}` | [x] |\n| 2 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 1..7` (every `switch (len-i)` fall-through case), random bytes ×256/len | [x] |\n| 3 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 1..7` with byte 3 / byte 6 forced `>= 0x80` (sign-extension quirk of `d[3] << 24`) | [x] |\n| 4 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 8` exactly (one full siphash block, `len-i == 0`) | [x] |\n| 5 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 9..15` (one block + each remainder), random ×64 each | [x] |\n| 6 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 16, 24, 32` (exact multiples, `len-i == 0`) | [x] |\n| 7 | `stbds_hash_bytes` | `len = 17..64` random, all bytes `0x00`, all `0xFF`, and random — covers `d[3]`/`d[7]` high-bit in the *loop* body | [x] |\n| 8 | `stbds_hash_string` | `\"\"`, `\"a\"`, 1..64 random ASCII, 1..64 random bytes `0x80..0xFF`, seeds ×8 | [x] |\n| 9 | `stbds_rand_seed` + `stbds_hash_bytes` | seed set to `0`, `1`, `SIZE_MAX`, random; verifies the global is a *pure* input to later table creation | [x] |\n| 10 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `a = NULL`, `elemsize ∈ {1,4,8,16,24}`, `addlen ∈ {0,1,3,7}`, `min_cap ∈ {0,1,2,4,5,17}` — full cross product, covering `min_len > min_cap`, `min_cap < 2*cap`, `min_cap < 4` | [x] |\n| 11 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | non-NULL `a` (grown once), re-grown with `addlen ∈ {0,1,cap,cap+1}`, `min_cap ∈ {0,cap-1,cap,cap+1,4*cap}` — covers the doubling branch and the no-op branch | [x] |\n| 12 | `stbds_arrgrowf` | `elemsize = 0` (header-only allocation) | [x] |\n| 13 | `stbds_arrgrowf` → `stbds_arrfreef` | grow then free; round-trip on a live pointer | [x] |\n| 14 | `stbds_hmput_default` | `a = NULL`, `elemsize ∈ {4,8,16,24}` | [x] |\n| 15 | `stbds_hmput_default` | called twice (second call is a no-op because `length == 1`) | [x] |\n| 16 | `stbds_hmput_default` + `stbds_hmget_key` | default-only map (`hash_table == NULL`) then a lookup ⇒ `temp = -1` | [x] |\n| 17 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | `mode = 0`, `elemsize = 8`, `keysize = 4` (int→int), `n = 0,1,5,6,7,12,13,25,49,200` random keys | [x] |\n| 18 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | `mode = 0`, `elemsize = 16`, `keysize = 8` (i64→i64), `n` up to 300 random keys | [x] |\n| 19 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | `mode = 0`, `elemsize = 24`, `keysize = 16` (16-byte key, `len > 8` siphash path), `n` up to 200 | [x] |\n| 20 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | `mode = 0`, `keysize = 12` (non-multiple of 8: 1 block + 4-byte tail) | [x] |\n| 21 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | `mode = -1` and `INT_MIN` (out-of-range enum ⇒ binary) — must equal the `mode = 0` result exactly | [x] |\n| 22 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | repeated puts of **already present** keys (the found-early-return path), interleaved with new keys | [x] |\n| 23 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | keys chosen to collide in the same bucket (same `hash & (slot_count-1)`), forcing forward-scan, wrap-scan and `pos += step` bucket walks | [x] |\n| 24 | `stbds_hmget_key` binary | hits and misses over a map of every size in row 17, `temp` read from the header | [x] |\n| 25 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` binary | same as row 24 but `temp` written to the caller's `ptrdiff_t` (and the header left untouched) | [x] |\n| 26 | `stbds_hmdel_key` binary | delete the **last** element (`old_index == final_index`, no memmove) | [x] |\n| 27 | `stbds_hmdel_key` binary | delete a **middle** element (memmove + re-index of the moved last element) | [x] |\n| 28 | `stbds_hmdel_key` binary | delete **every** element in insertion order, then in reverse, then in random order | [x] |\n| 29 | `stbds_hmdel_key` binary | delete enough from a `slot_count = 8` map that `used_count < shrink_threshold` — but `shrink_threshold == 0` for `slot_count <= 8`, so **no** shrink | [x] |\n| 30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` binary | grow past 8 slots then delete until `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` ⇒ **shrink** (`slot_count >> 1`, seed + arena inherited) | [x] |\n| 31 | `stbds_hmdel_key` binary | delete/re-put churn until `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` ⇒ **rebuild** at the same `slot_count` | [x] |\n| 32 | `stbds_hmput_key` binary | put after deletes so a **tombstone** slot is reused (`pos = tombstone; --tombstone_count`) | [x] |\n| 33 | `stbds_hmput_key`/`hmget`/`hmdel` binary | randomized 2 000-operation op-stream (put / get / get_ts / del, keys drawn from a small colliding pool so hits, misses, growt