arena (`storage != NULL`) ⇒ dedicated block spliced in *after* the head, `remaining` preserved | [x] |\n| 46 | `stbds_stralloc` | drive `block` from 0 up to and past saturation (`block >= 22`, `blocksize` capped at `1<<20`) with 1 MiB+ strings | [x] |\n| 47 | `stbds_stralloc` + `stbds_strreset` | allocate N blocks then reset; arena fully zeroed, list freed | [x] |\n| 48 | `stbds_hmfree_func` | binary map (`string.mode = 0`), string DEFAULT map, STRDUP map (frees each key), ARENA map (`stbds_strreset` on the table arena), and table-less map | [x] |\n| 49 | `strkey` | `n ∈ {0, 1, -1, 7, -7, 12345, -12345, INT_MAX, INT_MIN}` + 256 random `i32` | [x] |\n| 50 | `intput` | `num ∈ {0, 1, -1, 7, 8, 10, 12, INT_MAX, INT_MIN}` + 256 random `i32` excluding 9 and 11; called repeatedly to confirm the global seed advances identically on both sides | [x] |\n| 51 | seed lock-step | `stbds_rand_seed(s)` then a long identical op-stream on both sides, verifying every table's inherited/fresh `seed` matches (the global is advanced once per fresh `stbds_make_hash_index`) | [x] |\n| 52 | `keysize = 0` binary map | valid-but-degenerate: all keys hash identically and `memcmp(...,0) == 0` ⇒ single-entry map | [x] |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
