le` | [x] |\n\n### Deliberately excluded cell\n\n`mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` on a table whose `string.mode` is `STBDS_SH_NONE`\n(e.g. `stbds_shmode_func(e, 0)` then string-mode puts) is the one remaining\ncross-product cell and it is **not differentially testable**: the insert takes\n`default:` and `memcpy`s `keysize` bytes of the key *string* into the element,\nbut `stbds_is_key_equal` then reads those bytes back as a `char *` and\ndereferences them (C L561). The address is arbitrary key data, so the C's own\nbehaviour is undefined and depends on the process address space rather than on\nthe library. Note the first insert into an empty table never reaches\n`stbds_is_key_equal` (it is only called on a hash match), so this cell cannot be\nhit accidentally by the other rows.''')\nassert s != o\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\nnames=set()\nimport glob\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob(\"tests/*.rs\")):\n    names |= set(re.findall(r'#\\[test\\]\\s*\\nfn (\\w+)', open(f).read()))\nallrefs=set()\nfor md in [\"CONFIGS.md\",\"ERRORS.md\",\"SYMBOLS.md\"]:\n    allrefs |= set(re.findall(r'`((?:cfg|err|d)_\\w+)`', open(md).read()))\nprint(\"refs not tests:\", sorted(r for r in allrefs if r not in names))\nprint(\"tests not referenced:\", sorted(n for n in names if n not in allrefs and n!='crash_child_runner'))\nprint(\"total tests:\", len(names))\nmd=open(\"CONFIGS.md\").read()\nrows=[l.split('|')[1].strip() for l in md.splitlines() if re.match(r'^\\| \\d+\\w* \\|', l)]\nprint(\"CONFIGS rows:\", len(rows))\nprint(\"unchecked CONFIGS rows:\", [l.split('|')[1].strip() for l in md.splitlines() if re.match(r'^\\| \\d+\\w* \\|', l) and '[x]' not in l])\nme=open(\"ERRORS.md\").read()\nprint(\"unchecked ERRORS rows:\", [l.split('|')[1].strip() for l in me.splitlines() if re.match(r'^\\| \\d+ \\|', l) and '[x]' not in l])\nprint(\"ERRORS rows:\", len([l for l in me.splitlines() if re.match(r'^\\| \\d+ \\|', l)]))\nPY","description":"Add CONFIGS rows 41b/5