{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hisefxky7phc4bpgnppo5njjtudz67eovmliol7thkvnie72nbba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Result\n\n**One real translation bug found and fixed**, plus full differential verification: **110 tests**, all passing under **both profiles × 7 different RNG seeds**, with **exact symbol parity**.\n\n### The bug (found by Phase C, row 3)\n\n`stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` — C computes `free((stbds_array_header *) NULL - 1)` = `free((void *) -32)` and segfaults; the Rust used `ptr::offset(-1)` and aborted instead. C does plain **wrapping** pointer/integer arithmetic everywhere, so I converted every such site in the library:\n\n| file | sites |\n|---|---|\n| `src/types.rs` | `stbds_header`, `STBDS_HASH_TO_ARR`, `STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH`, `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD` |\n| `src/hash.rs` | `(t+1)` address math, threshold sums, `slot_count-1`, probe stepping, byte/string walks |\n| `src/hmap.rs` | bucket indexing, `used_count`/`tombstone_count`/`length` updates, `i-1`, `hash += 2`, `step +=` |\n| `src/arena.rs`, `src/api.rs`, `src/arr.rs` | `strlen+1`, `remaining -= len`, element indexing, buffer writes |\n\nThis also made `size_t` under/overflow match C (`ERRORS.md` #22 `used_count` wrapping to `SIZE_MAX`, #49 `elemsize*min_cap` wrapping).\n\n### Phase A artifacts\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 16/16 symbols identical (no missing, no extra), both profiles; plus struct-layout parity table.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 50 rows, mechanically grepped from every `STBDS_ASSERT`, `return -1/0/a`, null check and min/max constant. All `[x]`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 56 rows over the real branch axes (`mode` × `string.mode` × handle state × `elemsize`/`keysize`/`keyoffset` × counts × probe shape × delete/rebuild/shrink/tombstone × arena block growth). All `[x]`.\n- **`run_all.sh`** — derives the feature powerset from `Cargo.toml` (exactly **one** combination: no `[features]`, no `build.rs`, no `#ifdef` in the C, no CMake options) and runs check + suite + symbol diff for every combination × profile.\n\n### Notable C quirks confirmed reproduced\n\n- siphash `int`-promotion sign extension of `d[3]<<24` / `d[7]<<24` — verified **exhaustively** (every byte value in every position, `len` 0–17).\n- `stbds_hmput_key`'s **forward-scan vs wrap-scan asymmetry**: the forward branch sets `temp_key`, the wrap branch does not (`cfg_41b`, built deterministically).\n- `if (hash < 2) hash += 2` — reached by solving for a seed that makes `hash_string(\"\")` return exactly 0 or 1; 0→**2**, 1→**3**.\n- `intput(9)` and `intput(11)` **abort** at `lib.c:955` — byte-identical glibc assert text.\n- `(unsigned char) mode` truncation in `stbds_shmode_func`: 257→1, 258→2, 259→3 **alias** the valid modes; everything else hits `default:`.\n\nTwo things I explicitly documented as *not* differentially testable rather than faking: `elemsize>0 && keysize==0`-violating combinations that are out-of-bounds heap writes by construction, and string-`mode` on a `STBDS_SH_NONE` table (C dereferences key bytes as a `char*`).\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (md5s unchanged; only the sanctioned `c_src/build/` was added).\n\nOne caveat: the fatal rows that are raw NULL dereferences (`ERRORS.md` #29, #33, #48, #50) match **exactly** in release, but a debug build's `-C debug-assertions` `ub_checks` convert the SIGSEGV to SIGABRT before the faulting access — a build-flag artifact, so those four require exact equality only when `!cfg!(debug_assertions)` (documented in `ERRORS.md`). Separately, an independent read-only semantic audit agent I dispatched is still running; I'll relay anything it turns up."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":397860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1249,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0a431b9-dd3c-4caf-92f8-2cde17342eee","uuid":"19c717f7-9a5a-444a-aebc-9c6bbdd3628e","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11:46:42.189Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gryn2xklbpl73rozgby3njywra5ez7wrz3dvwuglhqfvogjyt7ra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the read-through plus an independent empirical differential audit. Here are my findings.\n\n## Findings\n\n**All 23 C functions have Rust counterparts and I found ZERO real behavioural differences.** Below are the 12 concrete non-identities I found, all of which I verified to be benign, plus the per-function equivalence list.\n\n### 1. C:832 `STBDS_ASSERT(table->used_count >= 0)` has no Rust counterpart — BENIGN (verified dead in C)\n`src/hmap.rs:472` replaces it with a comment. `used_count` is `size_t`, so `>= 0` is a tautology. I compiled `c_src/src/lib.c` with gcc 11.5 `-O0` and confirmed the assert is *completely* eliminated: the object file contains no `\"table->used_count >= 0\"` string, and `objdump` shows exactly **9** `__assert_fail` call sites with line arguments `0x191,0x30a,0x33c,0x34e,0x351,0x391,0x3b9,0x3ba,0x3bb` = **401, 778, 828, 846, 849, 913, 953, 954, 955** — line 832 is absent. The Rust has exactly those 9 `stbds_assert!` sites (`hash.rs:112`, `hmap.rs:375/463/520/523`, `arena.rs:76`, `api.rs:131/137/143`).\n\n### 2. All 9 assert expression strings / lines / function names match byte-for-byte — EQUIVALENT\n`strings` on the C `.o` yields exactly: `t->used_count_threshold + t->tombstone_count_threshold < t->slot_count`, `(size_t) i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a)`, `slot < (ptrdiff_t) table->slot_count`, `slot >= 0`, `b->index[i] == final_index`, `len <= a->remaining`, `hmget(intmap, 9) == num`, `hmget(intmap, 11) == 3`, `hmget(intmap, num) == 7`, and 5 `__PRETTY_FUNCTION__` entries (`stbds_make_hash_index`, `stbds_hmput_key`, `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_stralloc`, `intput`). Every string in the Rust matches, including the `stbds_arrcap(a)` spelling being *unexpanded* (correct: `#expr` suppresses macro expansion of the `assert` argument). `cffi.rs:31` reproduces `__FILE__` as the absolute path, which matches what CMake actually passes (`/local/.../translated_rust/c_src/src/lib.c`). **Runtime-verified:** `intput(9)` and `intput(11)` abort with *byte-identical* stderr and status 134 in C, Rust-debug, and Rust-release.\n\n### 3. `stbds_hmget` macro re-reads `stbds_temp` twice in C, once in Rust — BENIGN\nC `stbds_hmget(t,k)` = `stbds_hmgetp` → `((void) stbds_hmgeti(t,k), &(t)[stbds_temp((t)-1)])->value`, so `stbds_temp` is read twice (once inside `stbds_hmgeti`, discarded via `(void)`). `src/api.rs:104` reads it once. Pure load with no side effect and nothing mutates `temp` in between → no observable difference. (`hmput` in `src/api.rs:84,86` *does* correctly read it twice, matching C:135-136.)\n\n### 4. `ptrdiff_t temp` uninitialized in C:661, initialized to 0 in Rust — BENIGN\n`src/hmap.rs:197` `let mut temp: isize = 0;`. `stbds_hmget_key_ts` writes `*temp` on every path (a==NULL / table==0 / slot<0 / found), so the initializer is never observable.\n\n### 5. C:278/281 `stbds_array_header temp={0}; (void) sizeof(temp);` has no Rust counterpart — BENIGN\n`src/arr.rs:19` documents the omission. Dead local, `sizeof` operand unevaluated.\n\n### 6. `stbds_stralloc` shift: C `<<` vs Rust `wrapping_shl` — BENIGN (unreachable)\nC:888 `(size_t)512u << (blocksize>>1)` is UB for a shift count ≥ 64; `src/arena.rs:36` uses `wrapping_shl` (masks to 6 bits, which is what x86-64 `shl` does anyway). Unreachable: `a->block` saturates at 22 because C:890 stops incrementing once `512<<(b>>1) >= 1<<20`, so the shift count never exceeds 11. Verified over 3000 `stralloc` calls with mixed small/huge strings — `remaining`, `block`, `mode`, block-list length, and returned string all matched.\n\n### 7. C `t->string = ot->string` (struct assign) vs Rust `ptr::copy_nonoverlapping` — BENIGN\n`src/hash.rs:120-124` copies all 24 bytes including the 6 padding bytes after `mode`; C may or may not copy padding. Padding is never read.\n\n### 8. `stbds_hash_index::temp_key` is left uninitialized by `stbds_make_hash_index` in BOTH — FAITHFUL (upstream stb_ds quirk)\nNeither C:385-472 nor `src/hash.rs:82-200` ever initialize `temp_key`, and it is *not* copied from `ot` on grow/shrink/rebuild. So after any table resize, `stbds_temp_key` reads malloc garbage in both implementations. My first harness pass flagged this as a \"mismatch\" until I realized it is genuinely uninitialized on both sides. Correctly reproduced.\n\n### 9. C:495 `typedef int STBDS_SIPHASH_2_4_can_only_be_used_in_64_bit_builds[...]` has no Rust counterpart — BENIGN on the target\nThis is a compile-time static assertion that `sizeof(size_t)==8`. The Rust has no equivalent guard, so on a 32-bit target the Rust would silently compile (with `STBDS_SIZE_T_BITS==32` and `0x0706050403020100u64 as usize` truncating) where the C refuses to build. Irrelevant for x86-64 LP64.\n\n### 10. Release-profile symbol-interposition surface is smaller — BENIGN / theoretical\nIn the C `.so`, every internal call to an exported helper goes through the PLT (`readelf -r` shows 8 `JUMP_SLOT` relocs: `stbds_arrgrowf`, `stbds_hash_bytes`, `stbds_hash_string`, `stbds_stralloc`, `stbds_strreset`, `stbds_hmget_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts`, `stbds_hmput_key`), so they are `LD_PRELOAD`-interposable. The Rust **debug** `.so` has exactly the same 8 symbols as `GLOB_DAT` GOT-indirect calls — interposition preserved. The Rust **release** `.so` only has 3 (`stbds_stralloc`, `stbds_hash_bytes`, `stbds_hmput_key`); the other 5 became direct calls. Only observable to code that interposes stb_ds symbols; no semantic difference for any normal caller.\n\n### 11. Rust-only helpers with no C counterpart — BENIGN\n`hash.rs:17/22` (`hash_seed_get/set` around an `AtomicUsize` modelling `static size_t stbds_hash_seed`, relaxed ordering, single-threaded RMW sequence identical), `hmap.rs:62-65` (`stbds_strreset_local` trivial wrapper), `types.rs` accessor fns for the C macros, `types.rs:81` `STBDS_SH_NONE` (defined but unused, matching the C enum). `hmap.rs:373 let _ = raw_a;` mirrors C:776 where `raw_a` is likewise assigned and never used.\n\n### 12. Struct layout — EXACT MATCH (computed on both sides)\nI compiled a C `offsetof`/`sizeof` probe:\n\n| struct | C size/align | C offsets | Rust (`#[repr(C)]`) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `stbds_array_header` | 32 / 8 | 0, 8, 16, 24 | `types.rs:11-17` ✓ (`HEADER_SIZE`=32) |\n| `stbds_string_block` | 16 / 8 | next 0, storage 8 | `types.rs:22-26` ✓ |\n| `stbds_string_arena` | 24 / 8 | 0, 8, block 16, mode 17 | `types.rs:31-37` ✓ |\n| `stbds_hash_bucket` | 128 / 8 | hash 0, index 64 | `types.rs:42-46` ✓ |\n| `stbds_hash_index` | 104 / 8 | 0,8,16,24,32,40,48,56,64, string 72, storage 96 | `types.rs:51-64` ✓ |\n\nConstants all match: `BUCKET_LENGTH=8`, `BUCKET_SHIFT=3`, `BUCKET_MASK=7`, `CACHE_LINE_SIZE=64`, `INDEX_EMPTY=-1`, `INDEX_DELETED=-2`, `HASH_EMPTY=0`, `HASH_DELETED=1`, `HM_BINARY=0`, `HM_STRING=1`, `SH_NONE/DEFAULT/STRDUP/ARENA = 0/1/2/3`, `BLOCKSIZE_MIN=512`, `BLOCKSIZE_MAX=1<<20`, `SIPHASH_C_ROUNDS=2`, `SIPHASH_D_ROUNDS=4`, siphash IVs `0x736f6d65/0x70736575`, `0x646f7261/0x6e646f6d`, `0x6c796765/0x6e657261`, `0x74656462/0x79746573`, `0x0706050403020100`, `0x0f0e0d0c0b0a0908`, `load_32_or_64` magic `2147001325/0x27bb2ee6/0x87b0b0fd` and `715136305/0/0xb504f32d` (I hand-evaluated both: they yield `0x27bb2ee687b0b0fd` and `0xb504f32d` in both implementations).\n\n## Per-function verdicts (all fully equivalent)\n\n| C | Rust | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `stbds_arrgrowf` L276-310 | `arr.rs:13-58` | Equivalent. `ptrdiff_t+size_t`→`(as usize).wrapping_add`, `2*cap` wrapping, `realloc(NULL,…)` for `a==NULL`, `b = (char*)b + 32` wrapping (so an OOM `realloc` gives the same wild write). |\n| `stbds_arrfreef` L312-315 | `arr.rs:64-66` | Equivalent; `wrapping_sub` reproduces `free((void*)-32)` for NULL. Verified: both segfault (139). |\n| `stbds_rand_seed` L355-358 | `hash.rs:30-32` | Equivalent. |\n| `stbds_load_32_or_64` L360-363 | `hash.rs:44-55` | Equivalent; comma-sequence order preserved exactly. |\n| `stbds_probe_position` L367-373 | `hash.rs:62-64` | Equivalent. |\n| `stbds_log2` L375-383 | `hash.rs:70-77` | Equivalent. |\n| `stbds_make_hash_index` L385-472 | `hash.rs:82-200` | Equivalent. `ALIGN_FWD((size_t)(t+1),64)` == `t + 104` aligned; all 5 thresholds; `goto done` → `break 'place` correctly resumes the enclosing `for j` loop (item 5 in the brief). |\n| `STBDS_ROTATE_LEFT/RIGHT` L474-475 | `hash.rs:204/210` | Equivalent; all call sites use n∈{9,11,13,16,17,21,22,31,32} so `64-n` never degenerates. |\n| `stbds_hash_string` L477-491 | `hash.rs:218-234` | Equivalent, including the no-op-looking `hash ^= hash ^ ROTR(hash,31)` / `,11)` written verbatim (item 3). |\n| `stbds_siphash_bytes` L498-551 | `hash.rs:247-347` | Equivalent. Body loop: `d[3]<<24` computed as `i32` then `as isize as usize` → sign-extends, matching C's `int` promotion; the `<<16<<16` high half likewise. Tail: cases 7/6/5 cast to `usize` **first** (`hash.rs:314/317/320`), cases 4/3/2/1 stay `i32` and sign-extend (`hash.rs:324/327/330/333`); the `if rem >= 7 … >= 1` chain is exactly the C fall-through because `rem = len-i ∈ 0..7` always. `len << 56` preserved. |\n| `stbds_hash_bytes` L553-556 | `hash.rs:353-355` | Equivalent. |\n| `stbds_is_key_equal` L558-564 | `hmap.rs:15-35` | Equivalent; `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` signed. |\n| `stbds_hmfree_func` L571-584 | `hmap.rs:41-60` | Equivalent; STRDUP loop starts at `i=1`, then `strreset`, then free hash_table, then free header. |\n| `stbds_hm_find_slot` L586-629 | `hmap.rs:70-145` | Equivalent; `(pos & ~7)+i`, both scan halves, `limit` computed from the unchanged `pos`. |\n| `stbds_hmget_key_ts` L631-657 | `hmap.rs:151-184` | Equivalent; NULL path order `arrgrowf → length+=1 → memset` preserved (note this differs from `hmput_key`'s `memset → length+=1`, and the Rust preserves *both* orders). |\n| `stbds_hmget_key` L659-665 | `hmap.rs:190-201` | Equivalent (see #4