1, ±7, 9, 10, 11, ±100, -999, 10^6, 10^9, -123456789, -2147483647, 12345`. |\n| `intput` L945-956 | `api.rs:124-149` | Equivalent. Redundant `intmap = NULL;` kept; `hmput` passes literal mode `0`; `hmget` passes `STBDS_HM_BINARY`; `(int[1]){k}` modelled by a stack `c_int`; `sizeof *(t)`=8 / `sizeof (t)->key`=4; leaks the map exactly as C does. |\n\n## Empirical cross-validation (both `.so`s were already built; I only compiled read-only harnesses in `$TMPDIR`)\n\nRan 5 independent `dlopen`-based differential harnesses comparing the C `.so` against **both** the debug and release Rust `.so`, seeding both with `stbds_rand_seed` to keep the internal PRNG in lockstep, and comparing the full observable state after every single operation (header `length`/`capacity`/`temp`, all 11 `stbds_hash_index` scalar fields, `string` arena fields, `temp_key` string, and every `hash[]`/`index[]` slot of every bucket, plus element payload bytes):\n\n- `stbds_hash_bytes`: 6 byte patterns × lengths 0..40 × 6 seeds, **plus** pointer offsets 0..8 × lengths 0..200 (covers every `switch (len-i)` case and every sign-extension path) — 0 mismatches.\n- `stbds_hash_string`: 9 strings (incl. high-bit bytes) × 5 seeds — 0 mismatches.\n- `stbds_arrgrowf`/`arrfreef`: elemsizes 1..16 × 40 growth steps; plus `min_cap=(size_t)-1` overflow (C wraps to `realloc(NULL,31)` and survives — Rust identical) — 0 mismatches.\n- Binary maps: 4 scenarios up to 600 inserts + 1010 gets/`get_ts` + 333 deletes (exercising grow, shrink, tombstone rebuild) with 4-, 8-byte and struct keys — 0 mismatches.\n- String maps: `SH_DEFAULT`, `SH_STRDUP`, `SH_ARENA` × 400 inserts + 160 gets + 200 deletes — 0 mismatches; also `mode` 2 and 3 (`>= HM_STRING` but `!= HM_STRING`) × 3 arena modes, 77 648 lines of state dump — **byte-identical**, including the `mode==2` delete path which correctly aborts at line 846 in both.\n- Arena: 3000 `stralloc` calls mixing 1–40-byte and 600–3600-byte strings (drives `block` to its cap) + `strreset` — 0 mismatches.\n- Degenerate entry points: `hmdel_key(NULL)`, `hmget_key_ts(NULL)`, `table==0` paths, `hmput_default(NULL)`, `hmfree_func(NULL)`, `strreset` on a zeroed arena, `arrfreef(NULL)` (both SIGSEGV), nonzero `keyoffset` on delete — 0 mismatches.\n- `intput` for 10 values incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` and the aborting `9`/`11` — identical stdout/stderr/exit status.\n\nAlso confirmed the Rust contains no `panic!`/`unwrap`/`expect`/`assert!`/indexing that could trap where C would not (I checked every `+=`/`+`/`<<`/`[]` site: shift counts are all literal and in range, `digits[10]` is exactly wide enough for `INT_MIN`, bucket indices are all masked to 0..7), so the debug profile (which lacks `panic = \"abort\"`) has no reachable unwind-across-FFI site.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Real behavioural differences found: 0.**\n\n12 non-identities were identified and each was shown to be benign: 1 dead assert (C:832, verified eliminated by gcc), 1 redundant pure re-read of `stbds_temp`, 1 harmless initializer, 1 dead local, 1 unreachable UB-vs-`wrapping_shl` shift, 1 padding-copy nuance, 1 faithfully-reproduced uninitialized field, 1 missing compile-time 64-bit static assertion, 1 release-only symbol-interposition surface reduction, and 3 categories of Rust-only glue with no semantic effect."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3944,"cache_read_input_tokens":144787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3944,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01HQSKqt7QTsaAuDELJmRc2h","session_id":"b0a431b9-dd3c-4caf-92f8-2cde17342eee","uuid":"666f4af3-bb97-4cc2-8b6a-7ffc44fabd46","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11:47:11.117Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Independent C-vs-Rust semantic audit"}
