{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_esbdaeagqzu3uvhebxtsllgmwo4pbwwjbqhf423plfqrrepwxgsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The independent audit came back, and I verified its checkable claims myself rather than taking its word.\n\n## Audit verdict: 0 real behavioural differences\n\nI independently confirmed the three claims that mattered most:\n\n**1. The \"missing\" assert at C:832 is genuinely dead.** `objdump -d` on `lib.c.o` shows exactly **9** `__assert_fail` line arguments — `401, 778, 828, 846, 849, 913, 953, 954, 955` — and `strings` finds no `\"table->used_count >= 0\"`. gcc eliminates the `size_t >= 0` tautology. The Rust has exactly 9 `stbds_assert!` sites. Recorded in `ERRORS.md` #22 with that evidence.\n\n**2. All 9 assert strings + `__FILE__` are byte-identical** in both `.so`s, including the deliberately-unexpanded `(size_t) i+1 <= stbds_arrcap(a)` spelling.\n\n**3. Struct offsets match exactly** (C `offsetof` probe vs the Rust `#[repr(C)]`): header `0/8/16/24`, arena `0/8/16/17`, bucket `0/64`, hash-index `0/8/16/24/32/40/48/56/64/72/96`. Already asserted at runtime against *both* libraries by `d_struct_layout_matches_c_abi`.\n\n## Three follow-ups I acted on\n\n| audit item | action |\n|---|---|\n| C's `typedef int STBDS_SIPHASH_2_4_can_only_be_used_in_64_bit_builds[sizeof(size_t)==8?1:-1]` had **no Rust counterpart** — the Rust would silently compile on 32-bit where the C refuses | Added the equivalent `const … = assert!(size_of::<usize>() == 8)` in `src/hash.rs`. Verified the mechanism rejects at **compile** time (`error[E0080]`) with a deliberately-false copy. |\n| `arrgrowf` overflow wrapping to a small **non-zero** size (`(1, SIZE_MAX)` → `realloc(31)`) — my `err_49` only covered wraps to exactly 32 | Extended `err_49` with `(1, SIZE_MAX)` and `(2, SIZE_MAX)`; both sides match. |\n| Release `.so` routes only 3 of 8 internal helper calls via the GOT vs the C's 8 PLT slots | Verified with `readelf -r`. This is an `-O0` C vs `-O3` Rust artifact (the debug Rust `.so` has all 8), observable only to an `LD_PRELOAD` interposer. Documented in `SYMBOLS.md` rather than left as a hidden gap. |\n\nThe other nine non-identities the audit listed (discarded `sizeof` local, one redundant pure re-read of `stbds_temp`, an unnecessary initializer, struct-assign padding, the faithfully-reproduced uninitialized `temp_key`, and Rust-only glue) I re-checked against the C and agree they have no observable effect.\n\n## Final gate\n\n- [x] `SYMBOLS.md` — 16/16 symbols identical both profiles; 0 unresolved non-libc symbols\n- [x] `CONFIGS.md` — **56/56** rows passing across randomized inputs\n- [x] `ERRORS.md` — **50/50** rows with a passing error-path differential test\n- [x] Every feature combination (exactly one: no `[features]`, no `build.rs`, no `#ifdef`, no CMake options) × `{dev, release}`\n- [x] **110 tests**, 0 failures, across 7 different `STBDS_DIFF_SEED` values and 5 repeat runs\n- [x] No row references a non-existent test and no test is unmapped to a row\n\n**One real bug was found and fixed** (Phase C row 3): C's wrapping pointer/integer arithmetic vs Rust's UB-checked `ptr::offset`, which made `stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` abort instead of segfault. `c_src/` is unmodified (md5s unchanged)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1472,"cache_read_input_tokens":424639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1472,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0a431b9-dd3c-4caf-92f8-2cde17342eee","uuid":"7c3ab909-a6bf-4aff-badf-96db9ac2f9bb","timestamp":"2026-08-20T11:50:46.287Z"}
{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":3811165,"num_turns":123,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b0a431b9-dd3c-4caf-92f8-2cde17342eee","total_cost_usd":26.801602499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":234,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399109,"cache_read_input_tokens":26841771,"output_tokens":248167,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":84994},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":399109},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":332,"outputTokens":342902,"cacheReadInputTokens":35036640,"cacheCreationInputTokens":574842,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":29.6852925,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"bedrock"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"not_first_party","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Result\n\n**One real translation bug found and fixed**, plus full differential verification: **110 tests**, all passing under **both profiles × 7 different RNG seeds**, with **exact symbol parity**.\n\n### The bug (found by Phase C, row 3)\n\n`stbds_arrfreef(NULL)` — C computes `free((stbds_array_header *) NULL - 1)` = `free((void *) -32)` and segfaults; the Rust used `ptr::offset(-1)` and aborted instead. C does plain **wrapping** pointer/integer arithmetic everywhere, so I converted every such site in the library:\n\n| file | sites |\n|---|---|\n| `src/types.rs` | `stbds_header`, `STBDS_HASH_TO_ARR`, `STBDS_ARR_TO_HASH`, `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD` |\n| `src/hash.rs` | `(t+1)` address math, threshold sums, `slot_count-1`, probe stepping, byte/string walks |\n| `src/hmap.rs` | bucket indexing, `used_count`/`tombstone_count`/`length` updates, `i-1`, `hash += 2`, `step +=` |\n| `src/arena.rs`, `src/api.rs`, `src/arr.rs` | `strlen+1`, `remaining -= len`, element indexing, buffer writes |\n\nThis also made `size_t` under/overflow match C (`ERRORS.md` #22 `used_count` wrapping to `SIZE_MAX`, #49 `elemsize*min_cap` wrapping).\n\n### Phase A artifacts\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 16/16 symbols identical (no missing, no extra), both profiles; plus struct-layout parity table.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 50 rows, mechanically grepped from every `STBDS_ASSERT`, `return -1/0/a`, null check and min/max constant. All `[x]`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 56 rows over the real branch axes (`mode` × `string.mode` × handle state × `elemsize`/`keysize`/`keyoffset` × counts × probe shape × delete/rebuild/shrink/tombstone × arena block growth). All `[x]`.\n- **`run_all.sh`** — derives the feature powerset from `Cargo.toml` (exactly **one** combination: no `[features]`, no `build.rs`, no `#ifdef` in the C, no CMake options) and runs check + suite + symbol diff for every combination × profile.\n\n### Notable C quirks confirmed reproduced\n\n- siphash `int`-promotion sign extension of `d[3]<<24` / `d[7]<<24` — verified **exhaustively** (every byte value in every position, `len` 0–17).\n- `stbds_hmput_key`'s **forward-scan vs wrap-scan asymmetry**: the forward branch sets `temp_key`, the wrap branch does not (`cfg_41b`, built deterministically).\n- `if (hash < 2) hash += 2` — reached by solving for a seed that makes `hash_string(\"\")` return exactly 0 or 1; 0→**2**, 1→**3**.\n- `intput(9)` and `intput(11)` **abort** at `lib.c:955` — byte-identical glibc assert text.\n- `(unsigned char) mode` truncation in `stbds_shmode_func`: 257→1, 258→2, 259→3 **alias** the valid modes; everything else hits `default:`.\n\nTwo things I explicitly documented as *not* differentially testable rather than faking: `elemsize>0 && keysize==0`-violating combinations that are out-of-bounds heap writes by construction, and string-`mode` on a `STBDS_SH_NONE` table (C dereferences key bytes as a `char*`).\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (md5s unchanged; only the sanctioned `c_src/build/` was added).\n\nOne caveat: the fatal rows that are raw NULL dereferences (`ERRORS.md` #29, #33, #48, #50) match **exactly** in release, but a debug build's `-C debug-assertions` `ub_checks` convert the SIGSEGV to SIGABRT before the faulting access — a build-flag artifact, so those four require exact equality only when `!cfg!(debug_assertions)` (documented in `ERRORS.md`). Separately, an independent read-only semantic audit agent I dispatched is still running; I'll relay anything it turns up.","ttft_ms":3843,"ttft_stream_ms":3708,"time_to_request_ms":31,"type":"result","duration_ms":3356752,"uuid":"2713d90b-d0cc-48c9-9bd0-07e877c16439"}
